{"BasePaginator and OptimizedCursorPaginator allow negative slice start indices (e.g. queryset[-10:20]), which Django ORM does not support and will raise a runtime error": 0.950531005859375, "organization_auditlogs endpoint accesses organization_context.member.has_global_access without checking if organization_context.member is None, which will raise AttributeError if member is not present": 0.8049969673156738, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key calls math.floor()/math.ceil() on the key value assuming it is numeric, but when used with datetime-ordered querysets (like audit logs with order_by='-datetime'), this will raise a TypeError": 0.9768537878990173, "Permitting negative offsets in Cursor violates the non-negative offset contract relied upon by all other paginator implementations (OffsetPaginator, CallbackPaginator, etc.), causing incorrect results or exceptions": 0.8802984952926636, "Cursor.from_string parses offset directly from user-controlled input without validating it is non-negative, allowing an attacker to craft a cursor string (e.g. '0:-1:0') that injects a negative offset into the pagination path": 0.8825392723083496}